 "answer": {
  "answer": "The study did not find a case of VaVAM rear-ending the lead car, and it confirmed only 3 of the 5 cases the brief asked for. Every case it confirmed fails in some other way. At S28 (19f339ba, +1 s, 0.5x) and S7 (096988dd, +2 s, 0.5x), the policy steered left into a car in the next lane. At S27 (12855a41, +2 s, 0.5x), it drove off the road to the left even though the route said turn right. Each of these settings rests on only three runs, so its range only just clears 0.5. Two points weaken the confirmations further: every S27 failure is flagged as a possible simulator artifact, and one S7 failure was a collision during log replay, not a policy action. Every contact with the lead car the triage describes happened before the policy took control, while the ego was still replaying the recorded drive. Adding 100\u2013200 ms of planner delay produced no failures on any scene where it was tried.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "At 19f339ba with the lead car shifted +1 s and slowed to 0.5x, every run failed. This was not a rear-end. With nothing ahead in its lane, the policy braked for no reason and steered left into a car driving alongside in the next lane. The policy was at fault.",
    "settings": [
     "S28"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "At 096988dd, +2 s and 0.5x, every run failed, but only some failures were the policy's. In two runs the policy turned left into a car alongside. The third was a box overlap during log replay before handoff, which was not the policy's fault. The confirmation therefore partly rests on a failure that was not the policy's.",
    "settings": [
     "S7"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "At 12855a41, +2 s and 0.5x, every run left the road. The route said turn right, but the policy drifted left toward the median barrier. Triage reads this as the policy's fault. Every one of these failures is still flagged as a possible artifact, because the ego ended about 4 m from the recorded path.",
    "settings": [
     "S27"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On the two scenes that failed, the failures appeared only at the later time shift. The same scene with the lead car shifted +1 s instead of +2 s did not fail.",
